# GPS-enabled navigation, for the half of the mission that happens outdoors.
#
# The same airframe, the same ROS 2 graph, the same detector. Only the EKF's
# position source changes: satellites instead of lidar scan matching. Nothing
# downstream is aware of the difference, which is the point - a drone that
# loses its fix on entering a structure keeps flying on the laser.
GPS1_TYPE 1
GPS2_TYPE 0
SIM_GPS1_TYPE 1
SIM_GPS2_TYPE 0
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
# Source set 1: satellites for position and velocity, baro for height.
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 3
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 3
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 3
EK3_SRC1_YAW 1
# Source set 2 keeps the GPS-denied configuration, so EK3_SRCn_OPTIONS or a
# transmitter switch can fall back to vision without a reboot.
EK3_SRC2_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC2_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC2_POSZ 1
EK3_SRC2_VELZ 0
EK3_SRC2_YAW 6
FRAME_CLASS 1
FRAME_TYPE 1
VISO_TYPE 1
